+      "id": "vulkan-cm1-fa-sparse-gather-hoist",
+      "status": "active",
+      "mechanism": "The coopmat1 FA kernel on the QSA sparse path (USE_SPARSE: prefill and gqa decode) resolved each gathered KV column from data_sparse before every K slice, V tile and mask pass, then issued the dependent K/V load with a full wait and two barriers per 16-dim K slice; the RGP proxy (c29 dense e4, c18 sparse decode) shows the kernel wait-bound (VGPR 129, occupancy 2/16, ~60% of cost in vmcnt/lgkmcnt). Now the tile's Bc gather columns are resolved once into shared memory (sparseColSh, 256 B) and K slices are double-buffered in kvsh (slice d+1 loads while slice d runs its coopmat, one barrier per slice). Same LDS values and coopmat order: bit-identical by construction. The K_DBUF spec constant is a ternary product (an && chain lowered to invalid SPIR-V). Always on under USE_SPARSE; dense paths compile to the previous code.",
+      "commit": "4acd2c85dbaaef478857c4ac977d29629bc8d775",
+      "protected_paths": [
+        "ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/flash_attn_cm1.comp",
+        "ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp"
+      ],
+      "anchors": [
+        "sparseColSh",
+        "K_DBUF"
+      ],
+      "evidence": [
